''Not to be confused with [[Lobsters]], which are similar in appearance.''

[[File:Crayfish Detail.png|100px|left|Crayfish detailed]]
'''Crayfish''' is a low-level food available to players. Eating crayfish heals 20 [[life points]]. Players need level 1 [[Cooking]] to cook a [[raw crayfish]], and doing so gives 30 Cooking [[experience]]. Players will stop burning this fish at level 30 [[Cooking]].

Raw crayfish can be obtained by fishing with a [[crayfish cage]], which can be obtained as a free sample from [[Hank's Fishing Shop]] in [[Lumbridge]].

[[Fishing]] crayfish is effective at lower levels as they provide decent experience.

==Where they are caught==
Crayfish are mostly caught at fishing spots wherever a "cage/net" option is available. However, they are exclusively caught at the pond next right next to [[Fred the Farmer]]'s farm, northwest of Lumbridge castle. They can also be caught behind the church in Lumbridge.

Most people choose to fish crayfish behind the church in Lumbridge. This is mainly due to the relative distance between the fishing spot and the Cook's range in Lumbridge Castle. Once a player has completed the Cook's Assistant quest, they are able to use the Cook's range which reduces the rate at which food burns when cooking on this special range.

